  "claim_boundary": "This development-tier protocol admits only the deterministic source-v3 campaign input after the cooperative official CLI launches two fresh model-free materializer workers and a third comparator, and their public, sealed-evaluator, and 192-by-3 action-conditioned potential-outcome bytes agree. The transferable validation claim is byte identity and deterministic owner replay, not process independence: local PIDs are self-reported receipts, process_independence_security_claim=false, and a malicious same-user producer is out of scope. Random draws are action-specific because selected_action is part of the environment hash; this is not a common-random-number design. Admission does not verify the future runtime order in which a pre-action receipt must precede selection of the actually delivered action branch and publication of the next user reaction. It does not authorize a campaign, model or CUDA execution, formal evidence, an unseen single-axis gate, an integrated Product Horizon, any Appendable, Readable, Learnable, Steerable or four-axis effect, human evidence, or production ACTIVE. Source-v3 has already appeared in reader qualification lineage and cannot be reused as unseen formal evidence. This protocol is Product Horizon-only and shares no estimand, N, protocol identity, or evidence claim with A1 reactive-source qualification or the A2 MSC budget line."
